      "date": "2026-05-11T11:45:33.000Z",
      "title": "Full year 2026 earnings: EPS exceeds analyst expectations",
      "body": "Full year 2026 results: EPS: ₹72.41 (up from ₹38.34 in FY 2025). Revenue: ₹97.7b (up 6.1% from FY 2025). Net income: ₹5.58b (up 89% from FY 2025). Profit margin: 5.7% (up from 3.2% in FY 2025). The increase in margin was driven by higher revenue. Revenue was in line with analyst estimates. Earnings per share (EPS) surpassed analyst estimates by 16%. Revenue is forecast to grow 5.5% p.a. on average during the next 2 years, compared to a 2.1% decline forecast for the Basic Materials industry in India. Over the last 3 years on average, earnings per share has increased by 46% per year but the company’s share price has only increased by 2% per year, which means it is significantly lagging earnings growth.",
      "keyDevTypeId": null,
      "source_url": null,
